From eb90182c5507cfbb160b1367c4b0ba7d2512c44f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WaleWangPW <396218656@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:54:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] fix(task): wire Task05 v2/v3 decoder into the
 absent-target release inventory

The previous candidate (225c022) routed ReleaseAbsentArchivedResourceTarget
through a sealed physicaldelete.Admission, but the real SQLInventorySource
loader rejected every task_resource_cleanup_jobs row with
trigger='archived_resource_reconcile' as ErrInventoryIncomplete, so no legal
release (which requires a retained v2 anchor) could ever pass the inventory
load. The mock-only admission tests used an empty cleanup-anchor set and
never exercised the real composition.

- selectCleanupAnchors now decodes v2/v3 rows via the Task05 canonical
  decoders and rejects any drift, malformed snapshot, or unknown
  trigger/state with ErrInventoryIncomplete.
- CleanupAnchor carries the full canonical identity (OperationID,
  SnapshotDigest, ResourceKind, ResourceID, TaskID, ManagedRootKey,
  AnchorRevision, Path, RepositoryID, Branch, HeadOID, SnapshotVersion);
  inventory.validate requires every validated anchor to carry it.
- Request.AnchorIdentity carries the same identity so the release admission
  can perform an exact-bound match. Execute short-circuits verifyAnchors
  for ActionReleaseAbsent and routes through a new
  verifyAbsentTargetRelease that:
    * locates the unique retained anchor whose identity matches;
    * walks every non-anchor inventory source slice so deduped path
      collisions cannot hide a remaining reference;
    * rejects overlap, drift, missing anchor, non-retained state, unknown
      workspace state, malformed v2, wrong digest, wrong operation_id,
      wrong resource_kind, wrong version, empty identity, and children.
- Service populates AnchorIdentity with every redundant header field.
- New composer_release_test.go covers the real composition: in-memory
  SQLite writer DB, Task05-built retained v2 anchor, real
  physicaldelete.New with NewSQLInventorySource. Asserts the sealed
  no-op success receipt and every typed fail-closed path with zero
  durable side effects on the anchor or the inventory.
